   "source": [
    "Provided with two blocks of code, one is a random number generator and classifier and another is a Decision Tree Classifier which classified the numbers generated by the earlier code.\n",
    "\n",
    "**CHANGE-LOG**\n",
    "\n",
    "The following is what I did to the code given. Number 4 is the deepest of all. It introduces a new dataset and the changes in the given code to accomodate this new dataset. It also tests different the impact of different factors related to decision tree on the classification work. The Decision Tree Drug Prescription System is also in number 4.\n",
    "1. I run the given code on my notebook which ran smoothly.*(Difficulty:<10%, Time spent: <10 minutes)*\n",
    "2. Adjusted the number of clusters to see their impact on the classification of generated numbers. *(Difficulty:<5%, Time spent: <15 minutes)*\n",
    "3. Used the given Decision Tree Classifier code to classify the generated numbers above and test the impact of tree depth(prunning) on the model classification accuracy.*(Difficulty: 20%, Reason:I struggled to know how to use tree depth in the code. Time spent: Approximately 2 hours)*\n",
    "4.  Found a dataset to perform classification on from Kaggle (drug200.csv). The description of the dataset is in the Markdown file named \"About drug200.csv dataset\" present in this folder. I Adjusted the code given to work with my dataset by following the following steps and perform various tests. Each step difficulty is described below\n",
