    "       - Replaced the synthetic dataset with a real-world dataset (`drug200.csv`) using pandas. This dataset contains features like `Age`, `Sex`, `BP`, `Cholesterol`, `Na_to_K`, and the target `Drug`.\n",
    "       - Loaded the dataset using `pd.read_csv('drug200.csv')`.\n",
    "         \n",
    "         *(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: Learned in the previous module, Time spent: <10 minutes)*\n",
    "    \n",
    "    2. **Feature Mapping:**\n",
    "       - Converted categorical features (`Sex`, `BP`, `Cholesterol`) into numerical values using dictionary mapping for better compatibility with machine learning algorithms:\n",
    "         - `Sex`: Mapped 'F' to `0` and 'M' to `1`.\n",
    "         - `BP`: Mapped 'LOW' to `0`, 'NORMAL' to `1`, and 'HIGH' to `2`.\n",
    "         - `Cholesterol`: Mapped 'NORMAL' to `0` and 'HIGH' to `1`.\n",
    "           \n",
    "           *Difficulty: 60%, Reason: I had to read the importance and procedures to do this*\n",
    "    3. **Feature and Target Selection:**\n",
    "       - Selected and declared features for training (`Age`, `Sex`, `BP`, `Cholesterol`, `Na_to_K`) using the code below\n",
    "          X = df[['Age', 'Sex', 'BP', 'Cholesterol', 'Na_to_K']].values\n",
    "       - Set the target variable to `Drug` using the code below\n",
    "          y = df['Drug'].values\n",
    "         \n",
    "            *(Difficulty:20%, Reason: Well described by the sources, time spent: Approximatelly 1 hour)*\n",
    "           \n",
    "    4. **Encoding of the Target Variable:**\n",
    "       - Since the target variable `Drug` is categorical, I encoded it into numerical values using LabelEncoder(). This allowed the decision tree classifier to work with the target data well. I used the code below:\n",
    "         y_encoded = encoder.fit_transform(y)\n",
    "         \n",
    "        *(Combined with 2 above, same weight and reason)*\n",
    "         \n",
    "    5. **Train-Test Split:**\n",
    "       - Split the dataset into training and testing sets with a 70-30 ratio using train_test_split() to evaluate the model’s performance. I used the line of code below:\n",
    "         X_train, X_test, y_train, y_test = train_test_split(X, y_encoded, test_size=0.3, random_state=42)\n",
    "\n",
    "        *(Difficulty: 30%, Reason: Took time for me to understand that line of code, Time spent: approximately 40 minutes)*\n",
    "\n",
    "    6. **Feature Scaling:**\n",
    "       - Applied standard scaling to ensure all features are on the same scale using `StandardScaler()`. I used the code:\n",
    "         X_train_scaled = scaler.fit_transform(X_train)\n",
    "         X_test_scaled = scaler.transform(X_test)\n",
    "\n",
    "        *(Difficulty: 70%, Reason: Took time to learn how to implement this for non numerical variables, Time spent: more than 2 hours)*\n",
    "\n",
    "    7. **Training our Model:**\n",
    "       - Used the DecisionTreeClassifier() for model training, initializing the model with random_state=42 to ensure reproducibility.\n",
    "       - Fitted the model on the scaled training data using the line of code below:\n",
    "         model.fit(X_train_scaled, y_train)\n",
    "\n",
    "        *(Difficulty: <10%, Reason: sources were clear about this, Time spent: <10 minutes hours)*\n",
    "\n",
    "    8. **Visualization of the Decision Tree Created:**\n",
    "       - Removed the custom visualize_classifier() function and instead used the plot_tree() function from `sklearn.tree` to visualize the trained decision tree.\n",
    "       - Plotted the decision tree with labeled features and classes, adjusting the figure size for better readability:\n",
    "         plt.figure(figsize=(20,10))\n",
    "         plot_tree(model, filled=True, feature_names=['Age', 'Sex', 'BP', 'Cholesterol', 'Na_to_K'], class_names=encoder.classes_, rounded=True, fontsize=12)\n",
    "       - Added plt.show() to display the tree.\n",
    "         \n",
    "         *(Difficulty: >70%, Reason: Took time to learn how to visualize a tree, Time spent: more than 4 hours)*\n",
    "         \n",
